## Fixes dcccrypto/percolator-launch#936 (finding 1)

Adds a defensive guard preventing the same account from being passed as both `dest` and `slab` in the ReclaimSlabRent handler (tag 52).

While passing the same account would result in a no-op (no fund loss), this is a defense-in-depth guard per security review.

```rust
if a_dest.key == a_slab.key {
    return Err(ProgramError::InvalidArgument);
}
```

**Note:** Finding 2 (trivial Kani proofs) is a separate concern — the existing proofs verify type-level safety, not handler logic. Can be addressed in a follow-up.
